00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:36.860
And now back to the show.

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:39.540
It's impossible to talk about
Succession without talking

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:42.830
about money because every
scene is basically drowning

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:43.990
in dollar signs.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:46.180
The Roy family are media moguls styled

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:47.760
after the Murdochs who Lord

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:50.320
over a vast empire
anchored by amusement parks

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:52.390
and a reactionary right-wing news channel.

00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:54.930
- You know Waystar, Waystar Roy Co.?

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:56.427
We do hate speech and rollercoasters.

00:03:56.427 --> 00:03:58.750
- {Michael} As a result,
they live in a world that

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:00.910
is totally defined by wealth.

00:04:00.910 --> 00:04:03.300
They wear the finest suits,
can take private jets

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:05.620
from luxurious penthouses
to countryside mansions.

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:06.940
They eat the fanciest food.

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:09.329
- That's so, that's so good.

00:04:09.329 --> 00:04:10.670
- {Michael} They drink the fanciest wine.

00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:12.803
- Hey Greg, what are you drinking?

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:17.844
- Oh, this is, I'm not
sure it's a, it's a, rosé.

00:04:17.844 --> 00:04:18.727
It's not my favorite.

00:04:18.727 --> 00:04:20.840
- {Michael} They have
extravagant leisure activities.

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:23.184
- Might as well just throw
a grenade at the pigs.

00:04:23.184 --> 00:04:24.610
- {Michael} Every single centimeter

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:26.690
of their lives has been tailor-made

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:28.410
to ensure they get only the best

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:29.400
of the best.

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:31.440
Taken as a whole, the
show paints a picture

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:33.620
of what it looks like to
live with all the money

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:34.550
in the world.

00:04:34.550 --> 00:04:37.350
Conceptually, it's a fantasy
we've seen, played out

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:39.570
on screen lots of times before.

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:41.100
From popular TV series,

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:44.060
like Dynasty, Dallas,
Gossip Girl, Billions,

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:45.070
and Big Little Lies,

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:47.010
to hit movies like Crazy Rich Asians

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:48.270
and the Wolf of Wall Street.

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:52.030
How the top 1% lives is a
major part of our media diet.

00:04:52.030 --> 00:04:55.050
Some offer a pure celebration of excess

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:57.420
while some cast a more critical eye.

00:04:57.420 --> 00:05:00.150
But pretty much all of them
give us the vicarious thrill

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:02.630
of watching the filthy
rich play with their money.

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:04.910
It's pretty straightforward
wish fulfillment.

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:07.270
Most of us live the
majority of our lives penned

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:10.460
in by bank balances that are
never as high as we'd like.

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:12.750
So it's no wonder we lust after the idea

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:16.170
of a life where all those
limitations just melt away

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:18.930
and we can do whatever
we want all the time.

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:22.020
- Look, here's the thing about being rich.

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:22.900
Okay.

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:24.303
It's (bleep) great.

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:28.550
Okay, it's like being a
superhero only better.

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:29.660
You get to do what you want.

00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:30.847
The authorities can't really touch you.

00:05:30.847 --> 00:05:33.717
You get to wear a costume,
but it's designed by Armani.

00:05:33.717 --> 00:05:36.230
- {Michael} There's a term
for this, wealth porn,

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:38.380
which describes a media
that exists primarily

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:40.640
so we can salivate over designer clothes

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:41.870
and luxe apartments.

00:05:41.870 --> 00:05:43.270
Apologies if you thought wealth porn

00:05:43.270 --> 00:05:45.090
is when a dude (bleep) a bag of money.

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:47.440
The term was coined by
journalist Gary Pool

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:48.400
in the year 2000.

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:50.250
It describes the fawning news coverage

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:53.500
of the uber wealthy in publications
like Fortune and Forbes.

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:54.600
The term caught on,

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:56.170
which makes sense considering shows

00:05:56.170 --> 00:05:57.900
like Cribs were at their peak.

00:05:57.900 --> 00:06:01.990
Never forget that Tommy Lee
had a Starbucks in his house.

00:06:01.990 --> 00:06:03.960
- Tommy Lee has a Starbucks in his house?

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:05.130
- Cribs baby, watch it.

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:07.117
- Like a whole Starbucks
with workers and everything?

00:06:07.117 --> 00:06:09.042
- {Michael} Shows like
Entourage and Gossip Girl

00:06:09.042 --> 00:06:11.460
were also pretty brazen about their desire

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:13.150
to provide exactly this sort

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:14.800
of economic escapism.

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:16.470
Happily framing every angle

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:18.340
of their characters, material wealth.

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:20.620
But the term of wealth porn
becomes more loaded when

00:06:20.620 --> 00:06:21.870
it's applied to media

00:06:21.870 --> 00:06:24.290
that's ostensibly lampooning this excess

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:26.770
while arguably just indulging in it.

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:28.310
The Wolf of Wall street and Billions,

00:06:28.310 --> 00:06:31.040
for instance, have both
continually divided critics as

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:33.050
to where they fall on the spectrum.

00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:36.160
So why are we so attracted to stories set

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:38.040
within societies upper-crust?

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:40.710
Most obviously, wealth
looks really good on screen.

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:43.250
From lush apartments to designer clothes,

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:44.990
to exotic locales.

00:06:44.990 --> 00:06:48.050
And the cinematography
typically luxuriates in it.

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:50.890
Cameras whirl to capture the madcap excess

00:06:50.890 --> 00:06:54.730
or glides serenely across
each perfectly manicured set,

00:06:54.730 --> 00:06:57.380
but that's not quite what
we get in Succession.

00:06:57.380 --> 00:06:59.050
Their apartments might be huge

00:06:59.050 --> 00:07:00.170
and their dinners might cost more

00:07:00.170 --> 00:07:02.170
than any car I've ever owned,

00:07:02.170 --> 00:07:05.910
but the world of the Roys
rarely looks all that desirable.

00:07:05.910 --> 00:07:08.090
Visually, this comes
from the guerrilla style

00:07:08.090 --> 00:07:09.360
of the cinematography.

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:12.580
The show uses free roaming
cameraman to create a voyeuristic

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:13.860
and low-fi aesthetic.

00:07:13.860 --> 00:07:17.220
This adds a DIY clumsiness
to a designer world.

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:19.890
It also avoids the indulgent poise style

00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:21.980
of most media about the 1%.

00:07:21.980 --> 00:07:25.060
One of the shows directors,
Mark Mylod, told IndieWire

00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:28.090
that when filming the Roys
in any opulent location,

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:30.040
he always makes sure the character

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:32.250
is leading the cinematography rather

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:35.450
than having a camera pan
lovingly across a fancy set.

00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:38.550
It's almost an anti-aesthetic
in terms of the craft.

00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:41.620
He says the show purposely
avoids depicting wealth

00:07:41.620 --> 00:07:43.230
as synonymous with beauty.

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:45.530
The frequently unflattering lighting shows

00:07:45.530 --> 00:07:48.640
every dark under eye circle
and wrinkle to perfection.

00:07:48.640 --> 00:07:51.380
And the beige color palette
becomes overwhelming

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:52.770
in its blandness.

00:07:52.770 --> 00:07:55.780
As series creator, Jesse
Armstrong describes, their lives

00:07:55.780 --> 00:07:57.840
are somewhat denuded of color.

00:07:57.840 --> 00:08:00.050
In short, for once being filthy rich

00:08:00.050 --> 00:08:01.980
doesn't look filthy sexy,

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:03.900
which to be clear, isn't the name

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:06.360
for a type of porn where
a guy grinds up on a

00:08:06.360 --> 00:08:08.050
big pile of dirt and twigs.

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:11.270
And importantly, the series
used on-set wealth advisors

00:08:11.270 --> 00:08:13.360
to help the cast fully inhabit the world

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:14.767
of the 1%.

00:08:14.767 --> 00:08:16.510
Grounding it in the day-to-day realism

00:08:16.510 --> 00:08:18.600
of life as a rich person, the show is able

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:21.620
to effectively de-eroticize
the whole thing.

00:08:21.620 --> 00:08:23.400
Well, almost the whole thing.

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:27.100
Brian Cox can still get
it anytime, anywhere.

00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:29.870
For example, one piece of
advice the cast received

00:08:29.870 --> 00:08:31.510
was about how they made their way

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:33.070
in and out of the helicopters,

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:35.230
which the Roys used like Ubers.

00:08:35.230 --> 00:08:37.120
You'll notice that none of them ever duck

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:39.180
the way we would expect most people to.

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:40.620
That's because when you've been traveling

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:43.130
that way since childhood
it's as natural as stepping

00:08:43.130 --> 00:08:45.450
onto a train or climbing into a car.

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:47.890
Which is maybe why Kendall
is so comfortable inside

00:08:47.890 --> 00:08:50.010
a helicopter, that he occasionally tries

00:08:50.010 --> 00:08:51.690
to drunkenly pilot one.

00:08:51.690 --> 00:08:53.550
Because here's the thing,

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:56.820
if you've been rich your
whole life, the idea

00:08:56.820 --> 00:08:59.930
of being rich just isn't
all that interesting.

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:02.230
Cinderella stories like Crazy Rich Asians

00:09:02.230 --> 00:09:04.700
and rise and fall tales
like Wolf of Wall Street

00:09:04.700 --> 00:09:06.950
are so effective because
they give the audience

00:09:06.950 --> 00:09:09.410
an avatar who enters
the world of the wealthy

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:12.140
with the same doe-eyed wonder as we would.

00:09:12.140 --> 00:09:13.580
Because wealth porn is really

00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:15.126
for those of us who will never experience

00:09:15.126 --> 00:09:19.280
that kind of opulence or
unfettered freedom in real life.

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:22.540
In contrast, Succession
demystifies wealth.

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:25.500
The show pulls back the
curtain to reveal the drudgery

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:28.730
and degradation required to
create this seamless luxury.

00:09:28.730 --> 00:09:30.320
Like when the Roys are getting ready

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:32.010
to have a decadent feast.

00:09:32.010 --> 00:09:34.520
Rather than simply having
their tasty treats appear

00:09:34.520 --> 00:09:37.890
on screen fully formed,
the show depicts every bit

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:40.000
of the painstaking work their staff takes

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:41.400
to prepare and serve it.

00:09:41.400 --> 00:09:43.900
And then Logan gets mad about a bad smell

00:09:43.900 --> 00:09:45.563
and orders the whole
thing destroyed before

00:09:45.563 --> 00:09:48.130
a single bite has been eaten.

00:09:48.130 --> 00:09:50.650
- And I don't want all this (bleep)!

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:52.830
It's sat around in the stink!

00:09:52.830 --> 00:09:54.807
Pizza, we'll have pizza!

00:09:54.807 --> 00:09:57.230
- {Michael} And so we get
to watch that same army

00:09:57.230 --> 00:10:00.260
of service employees clear
away a few rent checks worth

00:10:00.260 --> 00:10:01.490
of haute cuisine.

00:10:01.490 --> 00:10:04.130
And when Succession does
show a Cinderella story,

00:10:04.130 --> 00:10:07.160
it's not quite such a whirlwind romance.

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:09.360
Connor, whose best
friend is Ferris Bueller,

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:11.680
is initially paying Willa
to spend time with him

00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:15.650
as an escort before the two
of them decide to go steady.

00:10:15.650 --> 00:10:18.920
But even after the relationship
remains transactional.

00:10:18.920 --> 00:10:22.230
Willa shacks up with a
delusional rich guy twice her age

00:10:22.230 --> 00:10:24.730
because it's the only
realistic hope she has

